<%- include('../partials/head') %>
<section class="hero" style="padding:56px 0 48px"><div class="container">
  <span class="eyebrow">LIV Authorized Training Provider (ATP)</span>
  <h1>Partner levels</h1>
  <p>Every Authorized Training Provider starts at Bronze. Silver and Gold are commercial levels that LIV records on a provider's profile.</p>
</div></section>
<section class="section white"><div class="container" style="max-width:860px">
  <h2 style="margin-top:0">The three levels</h2>
  <div class="grid g3 mt">
    <div class="card"><h3><span class="lvl lvl-bronze">Bronze</span></h3><p class="muted small">The starting level for every authorized provider.</p></div>
    <div class="card"><h3><span class="lvl lvl-silver">Silver</span></h3><p class="muted small">A higher commercial level, based on the provider's prepaid commitment and record with LIV.</p></div>
    <div class="card"><h3><span class="lvl lvl-gold">Gold</span></h3><p class="muted small">The highest commercial level, based on the provider's prepaid commitment and record with LIV.</p></div>
  </div>
  <h2 class="mt" style="margin-top:40px">How a level is set</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>A level reflects the provider's prepaid commitment and its record with LIV. It does not depend on how many credentials the provider issues.</li>
    <li>LIV reviews a level with a recorded assessment, and a different person decides it.</li>
    <li>The conditions for each level will be published here once LIV has approved them.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2 class="mt" style="margin-top:40px">Where the level appears</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>On the provider's page in the public register and in the register search results.</li>
    <li>As a small badge beside the provider's name on the credential verification page.</li>
    <li>It does not appear on a learner's credential.</li>
  </ul>
  <p class="mt"><a class="btn" href="/partners#register">Find a Training Provider</a> <a class="btn secondary" href="/partners/journey">How the process works</a></p>
</div></section>
<%- include('../partials/foot') %>
